    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: 28px;">SAC Alumni News Roundup</h2>
      <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
        <p style="font-size: 15px;"><strong>Chris Bonanno,</strong> Fall 2012 (M.S.), is a staff writer with Florida Today in Melbourne, Austin, Texas.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;"><strong>Drew Lacy,</strong> Fall 2013, is an internal communications specialist at Abrams Learning Trends, Austin, Texas.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;"><strong>Ashley Kalita,</strong> Fall 2013, is an internal communications specialist at Embras US.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;"><strong>Allison Glunt,</strong> Spring 2010, recently received her master's degree in civil engineering and is now a PE trainee at Florida Department of Transportation, Deerfield Beach, Florida.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;"><strong>Brooke (Fisher) Hambright,</strong> Spring 2012, married Brett Hambright on Dec. 23, 2014. They are now a family of four, and Brooke is a membership marketing and event coordinator at Specialty Equipment Market Association (SEMA).</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;"><strong>Angie Lassman,</strong> (Minor in Communication), Fall 2012, is a weekend meteorologist/reporter for WFLA in Jacksonville, Florida.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;"><strong>Eric Savage,</strong> Spring 2014 (M.S.), is a vacation services coordinator at Starwood Vacation Ownership.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: 28px;">The Writers' Den Peer Tutoring Program Heats Up</h2>
      <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">By <span data-field="author_name">{{ author_name }}</span>, The Communicator</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">What skill is not only incorporated in every educational study, but also in every professional environ-ment? The answer is writing.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">Writing is not just the act of forming letters and words into sentences on paper. It is an art form that includes structure, meaningful content and purpose.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">Many students, however, do not view writing in this way.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">The Writers' Den aims to change that.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">Housed under the auspices of the Schools of Art and Communication, the Writers' Den is a student-volunteer-based, peer-editing service offered to all students at the Florida Institute of Technology. The program is run by the SAC, and it is a vital resource for students who are looking to improve their writing skills.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"We have needed this for a long time," says Joy Patterson, English instructor.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"Before joining the Florida Tech faculty in Fall 2013, Patterson taught at Melbourne Central Catholic High School. There was a writing service was under way for a year, but it was hard for students to find time to visit it and faculty members to volunteer hours."</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"Most universities offer a writing service that is sepa-rate from course tutoring, since writing is a required skill for every student, no matter their major."</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"While Florida Tech offered students help in the Writers' Den, it was not integrated into the Academic Support Center, the university did not have a formal writing center. This was a gap that the Writers' Den fills. It was the perfect opportunity for Patterson to bring her vision to life."</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"The Writers' Den opened in September 2013 with the support of the Schools of Art and Communication. It is a student-volunteer-based, peer-editing service that helps students improve their writing skills. It was the perfect opportunity for Patterson to bring her vision to life."</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"At first, tutoring was offered on the third floor of the SAC, but as the program grew, it moved to the second floor. The program has since served hundreds of students, and the Writers' Den has become a vital part of the SAC."</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"I personally enjoy writing, and I hope I can share that passion with others," says Patterson.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"The Writers' Den can be accessed at http://writersden.fict.edu/ or by visiting the SAC on the second floor. We welcome all students to stop by and learn more about the program."</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"An appointment can be made in advance, but walk-ins are welcome during office hours."</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"Natalie Dorfield, an assistant professor of English at the SAC, says that the Writers' Den is an invaluable resource for students, and it has inspired her to take on a teaching role at the SAC."</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"There is a definite need for a writing center with such a diversified student body," she says.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"Patterson is excited and extremely optimistic about the program's future, and she hopes to see it grow even larger."</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px;">"The faculty has been really supportive, and I thank the Schools of Art and Communication for making this possible."</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

